02775993,0.03543682,0.02303212,0.09148414,-0.04528078,0.09234503,-0.08859679,0.05759368,0.06021573,0.2055041,0.02670977,0.04306227,0.03639038,-0.03181875,-0.01234762,0.04980009,0.09906299,-0.01168495,0.01331466,0.03937288,0.01940482,-0.02118087,0.06964305,0.00546718,0.00468219,-0.05223615,0.02883205,-0.03879193,-0.00752867,0.06968927,0.00722506,0.08468482,-0.05119178,0.00215444,-0.01021118,-0.00948307,-0.00049807,-0.04069566,-0.0319294,-0.02817861,0.01312208,0.00345939,0.11899745,0.00849989,0.00710818,-0.03946185,0.01759341,-0.00763721,0.02122005,0.06530535,0.02400583,0.03284485],"last_embed":{"tokens":470,"hash":"1r4uoy6"}}},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"1r4uoy6","at":1786122228468},"key":"01_Projects/fin-app/CONTEXT.md#Halcyon — Context & Handoff#7. Current state: done vs. not","lines":[164,273],"size":8388,"outlinks":[{"title":"migrations/20260718000000_initial_schema.sql","target":"supabase/migrations/20260718000000_initial_schema.sql","line":9},{"title":"App.tsx","target":"app/src/App.tsx","line":13},{"title":"views/Login.tsx","target":"app/src/views/Login.tsx","line":13},{"title":"views/Onboarding.tsx","target":"app/src/views/Onboarding.tsx","line":14},{"title":"DataContext","target":"app/src/contexts/DataContext.tsx","line":15},{"title":"data.ts","target":"app/src/data.ts","line":36},{"title":"views/Accounts.tsx","target":"app/src/views/Accounts.tsx","line":44},{"title":"views/Dashboard.tsx","target":"app/src/views/Dashboard.tsx","line":53},{"title":"concept/pacingData.ts","target":"app/src/concept/pacingData.ts","line":77},{"title":"0,5)` positionally, and it can't be sorted at module load — `txnIso` lives in `period.ts`,\nwhich imports `data`) and **nothing dated after 07.17** (`txnIso` would resolve it to a *future*\ncharge).\n\nConsequences, all intended: the 12-month outflow total went **$21.8k → $66.4k**, so every\nExpenses/Dashboard figure moved (the 3M hero reads $16,466, was $9,548). **Rent is now `steady`\n(cv 1.2%)** and its \"+100%\" false alarm is gone.\n\n**Two follow-ups this did NOT close:**\n1. **Power still reads \"pacing over\" (+77%)** on a bill paid in full on the 3rd. It is correctly\n   `variable` (cv 15%) — real power bills do swing seasonally, and flattening the fixture to flatter\n   the tile would be the same \"fixture is fiction\" sin — but `landingFor` only projects *steady* rows\n   to their baseline and straight-lines everything else. Volatility was always a *proxy* for \"does\n   this arrive in one lump?\"; [lib/recurring.ts","target":"app/src/lib/recurring.ts","line":81},{"title":"INDEX.md","target":"INDEX.md","line":107}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
